# What the Integration test drivers run (run_correctness.sh run_performance.sh, tasks/run_tasks.sh). 
#
#   cp run.env.example run.env && $EDITOR run.env
#
# Nothing here is required: every variable below has a working default, and the
# whole file is optional. *Where the toolchain lives* is the part you do have to
# set up, and it lives elsewhere — ../../local.env at the repo root, shared
# with quick-compile/. Start there.
#
# Precedence: local.env, then this file, then anything exported in your
# shell or set inline, which always wins:
#   RUNTIME=libgomp DATASET=SMALL_DATASET ./run_correctness.sh
#
# Every variable and its default: README.md, "Configuration reference".

# --- What to run (the values shown are the defaults) --------------------------

# RUNTIME="iomp"          # iomp | libgomp | pmsis (PULP/gvsoc)
# SUITE="bundled"         # bundled: the kernels vendored in kernels/
#                         # full:    the whole external suite, which needs
#                         #          POLYBENCH set in local.env
# KERNELS=""              # explicit kernel list, overrides SUITE
# DATASET=""              # MINI_/SMALL_/STANDARD_/LARGE_/EXTRALARGE_DATASET.
#                         # Default: MINI for correctness, LARGE for performance
# THREADS="16"            # threads for the parallel runs; ignored on pmsis
# OUTDIR="$PWD/results"   # where binaries, dumps and CSVs land

# --- Performance only (run_performance.sh) ------------------------------------

# REPS="10"                # timed runs per cell, min+max dropped
# VARIANCE_ACCEPTED="5"   # warn if a cell's relative std-dev exceeds this %
# PLOT="false"            # true -> speedup bar chart at the end; needs python3 +
#                         # matplotlib, and picks up ./.venv automatically
